        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rudolf Kjellén, a German geographer and ethnographer\n- Organizations: Nazi Party\n- Concepts: Blood and soil\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Blood and soil was a slogan that came from this idea.\n- A German geographer and ethnographer became notable for first using the term Blood and soil in the 1940s.\n- Rudolf Kjellén was influenced by this German geographer and ethnographer.\n- The Nazi Party supported the most extreme form of the Blood and soil concept until the end of World War II.",
